  "caption": "Quinn's cartwheel ended with a landing on the shoulder and a broken collarbone. Sleeping in a sling became a whole new sport.\n\nCollarbones often heal in about 6 to 12 weeks in adults, and rehab is matched to the type of break and your doctor's plan.\n\nWhat often helps: use the sling for comfort, then wean off gradually as advised, keep the elbow, wrist, hand and neck gently moving, and let pain guide the pace. A bump over the bone is common and often shrinks over a year or so. If you smoke, quitting can support bone healing.\n\nTented or white skin, an open wound, a cold or numb hand, or breathlessness after a fall needs prompt medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
